{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Storytelling", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Simple Hansel ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.  Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.  Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.  Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.  Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.  Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.  Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.  Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reported Speech and Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use reported speech (indirect speech) when you are saying (reporting) what other people said. <br/>This style of writing is common in storytelling. It allows the writer to share dialogue with the reader without always using quotation marks.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you tell people what someone has said you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past' since we are reporting the information at a later time. You need to change the verb to the next past form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">love</span> him.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She said she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">loved</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'m coming</span> to the party.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">drank</span>.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had already</span> drunk.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> speak English.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> speak English.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You have to change the pronoun if you are reporting what someone else said. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\"", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>I said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  I said <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">I</span></span> didn't want to go.</li><li>Beth said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  Beth said <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">she</span></span> didn't want to go.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you want to report questions asked, the subject normally comes before the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Direct</span>: <span class=\"italic\">The frog asks Hansel \u201cWhere are you going?\u201d</span><br/><span class=\"underline\">Indirect</span>:<span class=\"italic\"> The frog asks Hansel <span class=\"strong\">where he was going</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When the question is a yes/no question, you use <span class=\"italic\">if</span> or <span class=\"italic\">whether</span> to report it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The father asks his sons <span class=\"strong\">if/whether</span> they have found wives.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below to see the changes in verb tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future Simple (will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Conditional (would)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal May\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Would\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "The frog asks Hansel where he was going.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Hansel explains that he was looking for a wife. The frog jumps onto a leaf and asks Hansel if it could marry him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The father asks his sons whether they have found wives. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Hansel explains that he was looking for a wife. The frog jumps onto a leaf and asks Hansel if it could marry him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I told you that Hansel was none too bright.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Use the Present Continuous to discuss an action that is going on at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. <br/><span class=\"italic\">People <span class=\"strong\">are pushing</span> them to marry.</span><br/><br/>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what occurred in the past and the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\">This tale <span class=\"strong\">has been told</span> by people in my family for ages.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without agents (the doers) are common in storytelling.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" am/are/is +  being + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> They <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are being pushed</span> to marry.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have/has + been + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> They <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been sent</span> out to look for wives.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "They have been sent out to look for wives. They've been told not to come back without one. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Like ... who hasn't been asked a question by a frog, right?", "type": "example"}, {"content": " He jumps for joy as he is being told that each of them has.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Each son feels that the beautiful wife has already been found. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So, the frog in the pond has been asked to go back to Hansel's house as Hansel's future wife. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Perhaps Hansel has been told the story of the frog prince!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "for ages", "type": "name"}, {"content": "for a very long time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This tale has been told by people in my family for ages. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a famous fairy tale.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "not the brightest bulb in the box ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not the smartest person around", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Hansel is not the brightest bulb in the box.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to push", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to use \u200bpressure or \u200bforce in \u200border to \u200bmove or do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are being pushed to marry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "frog ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bsmall \u200banimal that \u200blives in \u200bwater and on \u200bland, with \u200blong \u200bpowerful back \u200blegs with which it \u200bjumps from \u200bplace to \u200bplace", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The frog asks Hansel where he was going.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "none too bright", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not the smartest person around", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Hansel was none too bright.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "abode", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bplace where someone \u200blives", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He would give the family abode to the son who brought home the most beautiful wife.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to trek ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to walk a great distance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Simple Hansel says that, yes, he could marry the frog and treks home.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go online or to the library and find a child's fairytale.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Watch it and think about how the characters are being presented.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one character and write a paragraph giving a physical description.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In a second paragraph talk about what the character is like as a person giving examples of their reactions, behaviors, and life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your description aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I watch a child's fairytale.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about a character and a physical description.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about their character traits using the Present Continuous and the Present Perfect tenses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my description with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn9le08ob02re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn9le08ob02re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "This tale has been told by people in my family for ages.<br/><br/>There is a father with three sons. They are being pushed to marry. They have been sent out to look for wives. They've been told not to come back without one."}, {"image": "engenn9le08ob02re2img02.jpg", "time": "15000", "id": 2, "text": "One son, Hansel, is not the brightest bulb in the box. While passing a pond, he's being watched by a frog. The frog asks Hansel where he was going. Like ... who hasn't been asked a question by a frog, right?<br/>Hansel explains that he is looking for a wife. The frog jumps onto a leaf and asks Hansel if it could marry him.  Simple Hansel says that, yes, he could marry the frog and treks home.<br/><br/>The father asks his sons whether they have found wives. He jumps for joy as he is being told that each of them has. He says that he would give the family abode to the son who brought home the most beautiful wife."}, {"image": "engenn9le08ob02re2img03.jpg", "time": "59000", "id": 3, "text": "Each son feels that the beautiful wife has already been found. (I told you that Hansel was none too bright. He considers his frog a beauty!)<br/><br/>So, the frog in the pond has been asked to go back to Hansel's house as Hansel's future wife. (Perhaps Hansel has been told the story of the frog prince!) The frog is very happy.<br/><br/>Hansel has been given three keys and told to take them to a castle and take what he wants from the rooms they open."}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le08ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le08ob02re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about myths and legends.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that are being done or have been done. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can quote other people.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What are some popular fairy tales that children like to hear about today?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How are they the same or different from ones you heard as a child?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 